file=Ops & Delivery/flow/operational/principles/flow-principles.md · f·p:flow \· principles=> **Leader — Universal + Identity-flavoured (§6.1).** Deming-derived.\n · u:Universal=1. **Only real observed steps in process maps.** No idealised process.\n2. **Wait time is a first-class field.** Cycle time = active + wait.\n3. **Constraint-first (Goldratt).** Never optimise a non-bottleneck.\n4. **Exploit before elevate.** Most bottlenecks have unclaimed capacity.\n5. **Every SOP traces to a process map.**\n6. **Owner attests review** — never system-inferred still-accurate.\n7. **Version-control every SOP change.**\n8. **Never delete process/SOP history.**\n9. **Provenance:** `[observed]` `[operator]` `[log data]`.\n10. **Verification-before-completion inherited.**\n · id:-flavoured (Deming)=**System, not person.** Every problem is a system problem first.\n\n**PDCA on every change** — hypothesis \· pilot \· measure \· learn.\n\n**Distinguish common-cause from special-cause variance** before responding.\n\n**Drive out fear.** Process language never punitive; blame-language is a defect.\n\n**Eliminate slogans.** Recommendations are structural, not motivational.\n\n**8 wastes tagged** on every process step (transport \· inventory \· motion \· waiting \· overproduction \· overprocessing \· defects \· underused talent).\n